@b <https://example.org/lattice/mtp/legalruleml-cold2#>
@p lrmlmm=<http://docs.oasis-open.org/legalruleml/ns/v1.0/metamodel#>
@p ins=<https://www.nebularis.org/neuro-semantic/lattice/instrument#>
@p pty=<https://www.nebularis.org/neuro-semantic/lattice/party#>
%R Source fm mork:RDF lb "LegalRuleML deontic specifications"
%X
lrmlmm:Obligation RE
lrmlmm:Permission RE
lrmlmm:Prohibition RE
lrmlmm:Right RE
%T Concepts in Source
ObligationConcept C ra lrmlmm:Obligation
ObligationBearer C p lrmlmm:Bearer
ObligationAux C p lrmlmm:AuxiliaryParty
PermissionConcept C ra lrmlmm:Permission
PermissionBearer C p lrmlmm:Bearer
PermissionAux C p lrmlmm:AuxiliaryParty
ProhibitionConcept C ra lrmlmm:Prohibition
ProhibitionBearer C p lrmlmm:Bearer
ProhibitionAux C p lrmlmm:AuxiliaryParty
RightConcept C ra lrmlmm:Right
RightBearer C p lrmlmm:Bearer
RightAux C p lrmlmm:AuxiliaryParty
%M Scheme md mork:ReviewMode lb "LegalRuleML deontic specifications to stated LATTICE relations" sdl [lrmlmm <http://docs.oasis-open.org/legalruleml/ns/v1.0/metamodel#>] sdl [rdfs <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>]
Role_T MD xt pty:Role c role
Role_T_Label M cb Role_T xr rdfs:label r rdfs:label
Obl MD f ObligationConcept xt ins:Term,ins:Template c obligation-term
Obl_Relation MD cb Obl xt ins:Obligation,ins:Template xr ins:arisesUnder c obligation
Obl_Activity MD cb Obl_Relation xt skos:Concept xi ins:activity ct "activity/${rdfs:label}"
Obl_Activity_Label M cb Obl_Activity xr rdfs:label r rdfs:label
Obl_Obligor MD cb Obl_Relation tp Role_T f ObligationBearer xi ins:obligor
Obl_Obligee MD cb Obl_Relation tp Role_T f ObligationAux xi ins:obligee w 85 n "The auxiliary party is the party the obligation is related to. LegalRuleML does not say it is the creditor, so owed-to is read from the name."
Perm MD f PermissionConcept xt ins:Term,ins:Template c permission-term
Perm_Relation MD cb Perm xt ins:Permission,ins:Template xr ins:arisesUnder c permission
Perm_Activity MD cb Perm_Relation xt skos:Concept xi ins:activity ct "activity/${rdfs:label}"
Perm_Activity_Label M cb Perm_Activity xr rdfs:label r rdfs:label
Perm_Holder MD cb Perm_Relation tp Role_T f PermissionBearer xi ins:holder
Perm_Counterparty MD cb Perm_Relation tp Role_T f PermissionAux xi ins:counterparty w 70 n "An auxiliary party need not be the party that cannot demand otherwise of the holder."
Perm_Implied MD cb Perm_Relation xt ins:Prohibition,ins:Template xi ins:excepts ct "implied-prohibition/${rdfs:label}" n "Law I8: the permission excepts a prohibition on the same act, its obligor the holder." w 60 n "A weak permission is the absence of a prohibition, a strong one excepts it. The metamodel does not say which, so the excepted prohibition is always stated."
Perm_Implied_Term MD cb Perm_Implied xt ins:Term,ins:Template xi ins:arisesUnder ct "implied-term/${rdfs:label}"
Perm_Implied_Activity MD cb Perm_Implied xt skos:Concept xi ins:activity ct "activity/${rdfs:label}"
Perm_Implied_Activity_Label M cb Perm_Implied_Activity xr rdfs:label r rdfs:label
Perm_Implied_Obligor MD cb Perm_Implied tp Role_T f PermissionBearer xi ins:obligor
Perm_Implied_Obligee MD cb Perm_Implied tp Role_T f PermissionAux xi ins:obligee
Proh MD f ProhibitionConcept aw "lrmlmm:AuxiliaryParty [1..]" xt ins:Term,ins:Template c prohibition-term w 55 n "Prohibitions without an auxiliary party are not mapped, so the sample resell prohibition yields nothing."
Proh_Relation MD cb Proh xt ins:Prohibition,ins:Template xr ins:arisesUnder c prohibition
Proh_Activity MD cb Proh_Relation xt skos:Concept xi ins:activity ct "activity/${rdfs:label}"
Proh_Activity_Label M cb Proh_Activity xr rdfs:label r rdfs:label
Proh_Obligor MD cb Proh_Relation tp Role_T f ProhibitionBearer xi ins:obligor
Right_T MD f RightConcept xt ins:Term,ins:Template c right-term
Right_Claim MD cb Right_T xt ins:Obligation,ins:Template xr ins:arisesUnder c right-claim n "A right is several Hohfeld relations. Its claim end is an obligation owed to the bearer by the auxiliary party." w 65 n "A right also gives the bearer a permission. Only the claim end is mapped, since the permission needs a prohibition the source does not state."
Right_Claim_Activity MD cb Right_Claim xt skos:Concept xi ins:activity ct "activity/${rdfs:label}"
Right_Claim_Activity_Label M cb Right_Claim_Activity xr rdfs:label r rdfs:label
Right_Claim_Obligor MD cb Right_Claim tp Role_T f RightAux xi ins:obligor
Right_Claim_Obligee MD cb Right_Claim tp Role_T f RightBearer xi ins:obligee
Proh_Obligee MD cb Proh_Relation tp Role_T f ProhibitionAux xi ins:obligee w 45 n "A prohibition has no auxiliary party in general. It is mapped only where one is given (guard on Proh), because LATTICE requires an obligee."
